orphology\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Lymphoid Neoplasm (Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Plasma Cell Neoplasm (Multiple Myeloma/Plasmacytoma):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, arterial thrombosis, ascites\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n\nPlasma Cell Neoplasm (Multiple Myeloma/Plasmacytoma) vs Chronic Lymphoid Neoplasm (Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, arterial thrombosis, ascites\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm: bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Plasma Cell Neoplasm (Multiple Myeloma/Plasmacytoma): heavy chain disease, leukemoid reaction, neoplasm of mature b-cells\n\nRelated to Chronic Lymphoid Neoplasm (Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia): hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-